// Question: What is the difference between authentication and authorization?
// Write your answer below:
// Answer:

solution.code:
// Authentication = WHO you are (verifying identity)
// - Happens first; user provides credentials (username/password, JWT, etc.)
// - Handled by: AuthenticationManager → AuthenticationProvider → UserDetailsService
// - Result: Authentication object stored in SecurityContextHolder
// - Failure: 401 Unauthorized (via AuthenticationEntryPoint)

// Authorization = WHAT you are allowed to do (checking permissions)
// - Happens after authentication; checks GrantedAuthority list
// - Handled by: AuthorizationFilter for URL rules, AOP interceptor for method rules
// - Rules defined in: requestMatchers().hasRole() or @PreAuthorize
// - Failure: 403 Forbidden (via AccessDeniedHandler)

// Key classes:
// Authentication      → holds Principal, Credentials, GrantedAuthority list
// SecurityContextHolder → thread-local storage for the current Authentication
// GrantedAuthority    → represents a permission/role (e.g. ROLE_ADMIN)
// UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken → standard Authentication implementation

// Flow:
// Request → JwtFilter sets Authentication → AuthorizationFilter checks
// if not authenticated → AuthenticationEntryPoint (401)
// if authenticated but no permission → AccessDeniedHandler (403)

